from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
records=json.loads(Path('artifacts/design/design-sequence-verification.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
lines=['# Design Sequence Diagrams','','Version: 0.6 | Date: 2026-11-03 | Status: PIM revision for technical review','','These interactions realize the five customer use cases using the current detailed class contracts. The approved master template section is Chapter V / Detailed Design / Use Case Realization / Design Sequence Diagrams.','','| Use case | Editable master | Pages |','|---|---|---|']
for r in records:
 lines.append(f"| {r['use_case']}  -  {r['title']} | [{Path(r['master']).name}](../diagrams/sequence/{Path(r['master']).name}) | {len(r['pages'])} |")
lines += ['','## Reading conventions','','- Web entry: React Page  ->  concrete ApiClient  ->  HTTPS  ->  Controller  ->  injected service interface.','- Mobile entry: View  ->  ViewModel  ->  concrete ApiModel  ->  the same API contract. The operation-specific backend page supplies the detailed continuation; the Mobile page does not duplicate it.','- Runtime classifier names identify objects; `via I...` identifies injected contracts where displayed. Gateway implementation bindings remain as specified in the detailed class model. Frontend references use ordinary associations; DI is backend-only.','- Message parameters and return DTOs follow the detailed class signatures. PIM logical parameters exclude framework cancellation tokens and runtime wrappers. Explicit PIM-to-C# refinements are recorded in detailed/pim-to-code-mapping.csv. HTTP labels name contract operations, not selected routes or framework APIs.','- `[local]` denotes an internal computation within the current method, not a new public operation. TransactionWork is the existing callback contract.','- A single activation spans an invocation, its awaited calls and combined fragments. Alternative operands are mutually exclusive, not successive executions. The diagram has no elapsed-time scale.','- Responses stop at the UI; actor response arrows are omitted. The separate SePay webhook page is asynchronous relative to the customer checkout request. No callback is routed through CheckoutController.','- UnitOfWork calls back into the work scope and commits only after it completes; exceptions roll back. ProcessEventAsync evaluates the private table within that scope and does not start or commit a nested transaction. Notification calls occur only after a successful commit.','','## Source and design traceability','','- [Customer use-case descriptions](../requirements/customer-use-case-descriptions.md)','- [Stakeholder order/payment/return review](../requirements/reviews/order-payment-return-use-case-review.md)','- [Detailed class design](detailed-design-class-diagrams.md)','- [Analysis-to-design interaction mapping](detailed/interaction-to-design-mapping.csv)','- [Design operation traceability](design-sequence-operation-traceability.json)','- [Every rendered message and source-flow reference](design-sequence-message-traceability.csv)','- [Static review results](design-sequence-static-review.json) and [export/hash records](design-sequence-verification.json)','','## Review limits and unresolved issues','','The diagram sources and PNG exports are review artifacts, not an implementation or a runtime test result. Coverage here means representation of the current service operations and source flow groups; it does not assert exhaustive executable branch or condition coverage.','','The current repository contracts omit a dedicated non-locking owned-order detail read. GetOrderDetailsAsync therefore shows retrieval through FindOwnedAsync and mapping of the owned order data; efficient OrderDetail loading remains a contract review point. No nonexistent repository method or SQL implementation is invented. Profile uniqueness and validation details remain the responsibilities in the approved specification, without invented storage APIs.','','The latest stakeholder decisions govern initial order acceptance: acceptOrder precedes exactly one guarded Pending Unpaid/Pending Paid branch. No Pending Unpaid  ->  Pending Paid fulfillment transition is modeled. First unpaid orders require staff phone confirmation before approval, outside these customer interaction scenarios. Acceptance, initial payment, all-line FEFO reservation, order/line persistence and cart changes share the same outer transaction. The state-machine control pages are refinements of that execution. Persistence performed by the acceptance handler and SaveOrderAsync must participate in the same aggregate/unit of work, without duplicate inserts.','','Pre-acceptance payment-reference persistence/correlation, late or excess payment handling, prepaid cancellation refunds, outgoing payout provider and reconciliation remain TBD as recorded in the existing design. The verified webhook page indicates guards and fail-closed handling; it does not resolve these policies. VerifiedPaymentDto is a verification result, while HandleVerifiedPaymentAsync retains its current PaymentNoticeDto signature and must enforce trusted verification; review the trust handoff before implementation. Refund/return staff scenarios are not invented as additional customer use cases.','','The stakeholder authorized the table-driven state-machine replacement, storage amendment and ASP.NET Core C# migration. This is a reviewable implementation revision; release and external integration acceptance remain pending. Existing approved analysis diagrams are preserved.','','## Page and image index','']
for r in records:
 lines += [f"### {r['use_case']}  -  {r['title']}",'','| Page | Scenario | Source flows | PNG |','|---|---|---|---|']
 for p in r['pages']:
  lines.append(f"| {p['page']} | {p['name']} | {p['basis']} | [View image](../diagrams/images/{Path(p['png']).name}) |")
 lines.append('')
Path('artifacts/design/design-sequence-diagrams.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
inputs=['artifacts/design/detailed/detailed-class-model.json','artifacts/requirements/customer-use-case-descriptions.md','artifacts/requirements/reviews/order-payment-return-use-case-review.md','artifacts/analysis/sequence-traceability.csv','templates/Template_Requirements_Analysis_Design_Specification.docx']
Path('artifacts/design/design-sequence-source-provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps({p:hashlib.sha256(Path(p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in inputs},indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
